// A string is a sequence of characters everywhere, not only in the half of the
// family that happened to implement it. `count`, `slice` and `reverse` always read
// strings; `take`, `drop`, `first`, `last`, `rest`, `init`, `sort`, `unique` and
// `chunk` answered an empty *list*, so the mistake surfaced later and somewhere
// else as `upper expects a string, got list`.
//
// Each result keeps the kind it started with: a string in, a string out.
^ ⟨
  take: take("abcde", 2),
  drop: drop("abcde", 2),
  first: first("abcde"),
  last: last("abcde"),
  rest: rest("abcde"),
  init: init("abcde"),
  reverse: reverse("abcde"),
  sort: sort("cba"),
  unique: unique("aabbc"),
  chunk: chunk("abcdef", 2),
  empty_stays_a_string: drop("ab", 9),
  unicode_by_character: take("héllo", 2)
⟩
